---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Data With Duke">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20">
    <header class="mb-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-black text-blue-900 mb-6">AI Transparency & Ethics Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Last Updated: May 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate lg:prose-xl max-w-none 
                prose-headings:text-blue-900 prose-headings:font-bold
                prose-p:leading-relaxed">
      
      <h1>Is this just AI Slop?</h1>
      <p>
        At <strong>Data With Duke,</strong> we believe that data literacy is the ultimate superpower in the 21st century.
        To help you master that power, we use every tool available—including Artificial Intelligence.
        However, in a digital landscape increasingly cluttered with "AI Slop,"
        we want to be crystal clear about where the silicon ends and the soul begins. 
        This page outlines exactly how we use AI to build this site and create our content.
      </p>

      <h2>The "Duke" Philosophy: Human-in-the-Loop</h2>
      <blockquote>
        "We view AI as a high-powered laboratory assistant, not the Lead Scientist."
      </blockquote>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI assists</strong> with the heavy lifting (coding, formatting, initial research).</li>
        <li><strong>Humans analyze, verify, and write</strong> Every insight, conclusion, and witty remark you read here was forged in a human brain.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How We Use AI (The "Augmentation" List)</h2>
      <blockquote>
        "We use AI tools (like LLMs and automated scripts) to:"
      </blockquote>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Architect the Code:</strong> AI helps us write some of the code that makes this site run fast and look professional.</li>
        <li><strong>Research & Summarisation:</strong> We use AI to help parse massive datasets or summarize long
            technical whitepapers so we can find the "needle in the haystack" faster.</li>
        <li><strong>Proofreading & Clarity:</strong> AI helps us write some of the code that makes this site run fast and look professional.</li>
        <li><strong>Code-Pilot for Data Engineering:</strong> Our Python scripts and ETL pipelines are often co-authored with AI to ensure they are efficient and scalable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What AI Will NEVER Do (The "Hard No" List)</h2>
      <blockquote>
        "To maintain the integrity of our data storytelling, AI is strictly forbidden from:"
      </blockquote>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Generating "Original" Analysis:</strong> We never ask AI to tell us "what the data means." That is our job. The nuance, the context, and the critical thinking are 100% manual.</li>
        <li><strong>Fact-Checking:</strong> AI is notorious for "hallucinating" facts.
            We verify every statistic, date, and citation against primary sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Writing Without Supervision:</strong> AI helps us write some of the code that makes this site run fast and look professional.</li>
        <li><strong>Code-Pilot for Data Engineering:</strong>  You will never find a "fully AI-generated" post on this site. If a machine wrote it, it isn't a "Data With Duke" piece.
            This means blog posts, post comments, general engagement is all done by a living, breathing human.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sourcing & Data Privacy</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data Integrity:</strong> IF and when we use AI to help model data, we disclose the methodology used.</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> We do not feed sensitive or private user data into public AI models. Your privacy is a non-negotiable data point.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Promise to You</h2>

      <p>
        The goal of Data With Duke is to help you think critically. We use AI to remove the "boring bits"
        of web development and data cleaning so we can spend more time on the things that matter: <strong>nuance, evidence, and better questions.</strong>
        If you ever suspect a piece of content feels "robotic" or lacks the Duke flair, let us know.
        We value your trust more than any algorithm.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-blue-50 rounded-3xl border border-blue-100">
        <h3 class="mt-0">Privacy Policy</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">
          Like a well-rounded and slightly dizzy governance manager, you may have got here from our 'About' screen.
          We appreciate that AI and Privacy are often reported as nemesises... nemisii... opposites. But we promise to not use
          any of your data through interacting with our site with AI. We can't make the samer promise for 3rd party ads though,
          sp check out our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>